.venv
# Any nested virtualenv too. `.venv` alone matches only the top-level one, so
# backend/.venv (1.1 GB, including CUDA/NCCL libraries pulled in for local dev)
# was being copied into the production image by `COPY . .` — it is what made the
# image export run out of disk. Nothing in the image uses it: the container has
# its own interpreter and its own site-packages from requirements.txt.
**/.venv
__pycache__
.git
.env
*.log
*.md
mlruns.db
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
data/heart_disease/raw/*.xlsx
data/heart_disease/interim
data/interim
data/raw
data/processed
v2_archive
plans
deployment
scripts
reports/figures
*.png
*.csv
*.ipynb

# Exceptions: the heart model is BUILT in the image (no binary is committed),
# so its training data and build script must reach the build context.
!data/heart_disease/processed/uci_heart_by_site.csv
!scripts/train_heart_glm.py
experiment_files

# Gate 8.6-b: README illustrations. `*.png` and `*.md` above match ROOT-level
# files only -- measured, not assumed: a probe build showed
# docs/assets/research/fig.png and docs/guide.md both reaching the context.
# Nothing in the image reads these 1.4 MB of figures and screenshots.
docs/assets/
